tools.description:
[vectorcraft] Recolor Artwork
Location: Edit › Edit Colors
Params doc: {map: rows [{from: [colour keys (recolor.colors) or "#rrggbb" (every colour shown as that hex)], to: colour (hex, key, {c,m,y,k} or {l,a,b}) | null, exclude?: false (the row's colours are kept)}] | {"key or #rrggbb": colour, …} (one row per colour), method?: "exact" (default)|"preserveTints"|"scaleTints"|"tintsShades"|"hueShift" (how a row's colours take its new colour, relative to the row's darkest, average or most saturated colour), limitTo?: swatch library id or name, or "document" (the document's swatches): new colours snap to its nearest colour, group?: colour group rewritten with groupColors?: [colour] (default: the rows' new colours, in order, excluded rows left out), rename?: the group's new name, includeImages?: true, includePatterns?: true} recolour the selection (gradients, text, meshes, image pixels and pattern tiles included; each new colour keeps the model of the one it replaces) and the group, as one undo step → {changed}

[vectorcraft] Save for Office Documents…
Location: File
Params doc: {path?, ppi?: 150 (72, 150, 300… pixels per inch), transparent?: false (else on white), artboard?: 0} the artboard as a PNG for office documents and slides → {path, bytes, width, height} (pixels); no path → {dataBase64, bytes, width, height}

[vectorcraft] Save as Template…
Location: File
Params doc: {path?, compress?, version?, preview? (as document.save)} a native template (.vctemplate) that opens as a new untitled document; the document is unchanged → {path, format, bytes, warnings}; no path → {dataBase64, format, name: "<name> template.vctemplate", folder: the Templates folder (preference templatesFolder), warnings}

[vectorcraft] Distribute
Location: Window › Align
Params doc: {horizontal?: "left"|"center"|"right", vertical?: "top"|"center"|"bottom", bounds?: "preview"|"geometric" (default: the Use Preview Bounds preference; preview bounds take in strokes), patterns?: bool (Transform Patterns: pattern fills and strokes transform with the art; default: prefs transformPatternTiles)}

[vectorcraft] Distribute Spacing
Location: Window › Align
Params doc: {axis: "horizontal"|"vertical", spacing?: pt (the key object, select.key, stays put and the others are spaced from it), bounds?: "preview"|"geometric" (default: the Use Preview Bounds preference; preview bounds take in strokes), patterns?: bool (Transform Patterns: pattern fills and strokes transform with the art; default: prefs transformPatternTiles)}

[vectorcraft] Reverse Path Direction
Location: Object › Path
Params doc: {ids?, reversed?: bool (true: every subpath runs counter-clockwise on screen, false: clockwise, the Attributes panel's Reverse Path Direction On / Off; omitted: flip each path)} the paths in ids or the selection (groups and compound paths: the paths inside), as one undo step → {changed: paths}

[vectorcraft] Inverse
Location: Select
Params doc: {}

[vectorcraft] Clipping Masks
Location: Select › Object
Params doc: {}

[vectorcraft] All Text Objects
Location: Select › Object
Params doc: {}

[vectorcraft] Stray Points
Location: Select › Object
Params doc: {}

[vectorcraft] Open Paths
Location: Select › Object
Params doc: {}

[vectorcraft] Toggle Fill/Stroke Focus
Shortcut: X
Params doc: {fill?: bool (true: bring the Fill proxy forward, false: the Stroke proxy; omitted: swap which is in front)} → {fillActive}

[vectorcraft] Show All Hidden Attributes
Location: Window › Appearance
Params doc: {ids?, target?} make every hidden fill, stroke and effect (the object's and each item's) of each selected object visible again; errors when nothing is hidden → {ids}

[vectorcraft] Apply Graphic Style
Location: Window › Graphic Styles
Params doc: {name, add?: bool, ids? (layers too), target?: "object"|"contents"} give the objects (default: the selection; a group or layer itself, its fills and strokes painting its members and its effects applying to them as one piece; target contents: the objects inside instead) the style's appearance, opacity, blend mode, isolate and knockout, and link them to it (placed gradients land at the same place relative to each object's bounds); add: true (Alt-click) adds its fills, strokes and effects on top of the existing appearance instead and unlinks. With nothing selected (and no ids) the next object drawn takes the style instead (see appearance.newArt) → {newArt: true}

[vectorcraft] New Graphic Style
Location: Window › Graphic Styles
Params doc: {name?, id?} a style from object `id` or the first selected object: its appearance, opacity, blend mode, isolate and knockout (a group without fills or strokes of its own lends its topmost object's, type its characters'; placed gradients are kept relative to its bounds); links the object. Names are made unique → {name}

[vectorcraft] Duplicate Graphic Style
Location: Window › Graphic Styles
Params doc: {name} → {name}

[vectorcraft] Redefine Graphic Style
Location: Window › Appearance
Params doc: {name?, id?} replace the style (default: the one the object was last linked to) with the look of object `id` or the first selected object; the objects still linked to it update, and that object becomes linked → {name}

[vectorcraft] Rename Graphic Style
Location: Window › Graphic Styles
Params doc: {name, to} (Graphic Style Options; names are unique and linked objects stay linked) → {name}

[vectorcraft] Merge Graphic Styles
Location: Window › Graphic Styles
Params doc: {names: [name…] (two or more), name?} add a style combining the styles' fills, strokes and effects (each style's on top of the ones before it) with the first one's opacity, blend mode, isolate and knockout → {name}

[vectorcraft] New Swatch
Location: Window › Swatches
Params doc: {name?, color? | colors?: [colour] (one swatch each, in one undo step) | swatch? | gradient? | pattern?: name (default: the current fill), tint?: 0..100 (% of the global or spot `swatch`, or of the one the current fill links to), mode?: "gray"|"rgb"|"hsb"|"lab"|"cmyk"|"web" (convert the colour; lab: CIE L*a*b*, how spot colours are usually defined), global?, spot? (a spot colour, always global), group?: colour group name (solid colours only; default: ungrouped)} save a colour, gradient or pattern as a swatch. A tint of a global or spot colour (below 100%, without mode, global or spot) becomes a tint swatch, "Name 40%", linked to its base: it follows edits to the base and applies as that tint of it. Names are unique ("Sky 2"); a colour's default name is its values ("C=10 M=20 Y=30 K=0", "R=255 G=128 B=0", "Gray K=40", "L=55 a=60 b=40") → {name, names: [every new swatch]}

[vectorcraft] Delete Swatch
Location: Window › Swatches
Params doc: {name? | names?: [swatch or colour group names] (a group goes with its swatches), unlink?: true (art using a deleted global swatch keeps its colour, unlinked; false keeps the stale link)} delete in one undo step → {deleted, unlinked: paints unlinked}

[vectorcraft] New Color Group
Location: Window › Swatches
Params doc: {name?, swatches?: [names] (solid colours move into the group; gradients, patterns and None stay), colors?: [colour] (added as new swatches), fromArtwork?: false (add the unique colours of the selected art: fills, strokes, text, gradient stops and mesh points; a colour linked to a global swatch moves that swatch into the group), toGlobal?: true (with fromArtwork: the new swatches are global and the selected art's matching unlinked colours link to them), includeTints?: false (with fromArtwork: tints of global swatches also get swatches of their own)} → {name, swatches: [names in the group], linked: paints linked}

[vectorcraft] Duplicate Swatch
Location: Window › Swatches
Params doc: {name}

[vectorcraft] Sort by Name
Location: Window › Swatches
Params doc: {}

[vectorcraft] Swatch Options
Location: Window › Swatches
Params doc: {name, newName?, color? (e.g. {l, a, b} for a Lab colour), mode?: "gray"|"rgb"|"hsb"|"lab"|"cmyk"|"web" (convert the colour), global?, spot? (spot colours are always global), paint?: paint.setFill params ({color}, {gradient}, {swatch} or {pattern}) replacing the swatch's colour, gradient or pattern with one of the same kind} edit a swatch in any colour group, as one undo step. Fills, strokes, text, gradient stops and tint swatches linked to a global swatch take its new colour (at their own tint) and name; turning Global off unlinks them (they keep their colour). Colour, mode and spot apply to solid colours only; a tint swatch only takes a new name (edit its base) → {name, relinked: paints changed}

[vectorcraft] Move Swatch
Location: Window › Swatches
Params doc: {name? | names?: [swatch names, in order; or colour group names to reorder the groups], to?: index in the destination (they go before the swatch or group now there; default: the end), group?: destination colour group (default: the ungrouped swatches; groups hold solid colours only)} reorder swatches or move them into or out of colour groups, as one undo step → {moved}

[vectorcraft] Add Used Colors
Location: Window › Swatches
Params doc: {selection?: false (only the selected art's colours; default: all the art's), global?: false (the new swatches are global and the matching unlinked colours in that art link to them)} add a swatch for each colour used (fills, strokes, text, gradient stops, mesh points) that no solid swatch has yet, as one undo step → {added: [names], linked}

[vectorcraft] Merge Swatches
Location: Window › Swatches
Params doc: {names: [two or more solid-colour swatches]} keep the first (its name and colour) and delete the others; paints linked to them take its colour and link to it (or unlink when it isn't global), as one undo step → {name, merged: [deleted names], relinked}

[vectorcraft] Ungroup Color Group
Location: Window › Swatches
Params doc: {name: colour group} move its swatches to the end of the ungrouped swatches and remove the group, as one undo step → {swatches: [names]}

[vectorcraft] Spot Colors
Location: Window › Swatches
Params doc: {useLab?: bool (omitted: unchanged)} the document's Spot Colors options: spot colours defined in Lab show, print and export from their Lab values (true, the default: PDF Separation spaces get a Lab alternate) or from their working-CMYK equivalents (false: a DeviceCMYK alternate, matching older files). Art, gradient stops and tint swatches linked to Lab spot swatches take the chosen colour at their tint, as one undo step → {useLab, relinked: paints changed}

[vectorcraft] Edit Color Group
Location: Window › Swatches
Params doc: {group: colour group, colors: [colour] (hex, key, {c,m,y,k} or {l,a,b}; the group's swatches take them in order, extra colours become new swatches, swatches past the end are removed; built-in swatches can't change), rename?: new group name} rewrite a colour group as one undo step; art linked to its global swatches takes their new colours (and keeps its colour, unlinked, when its swatch goes) → {name, swatches: [names], relinked}

[vectorcraft] Make Opacity Mask
Location: Window › Transparency
Params doc: {ids?, clip?, invert?} the topmost of the selected objects (or of `ids`) becomes the mask of the others (grouped if several). One object gets an empty mask and enters mask editing: draw the mask, then transparency.stopEditingOpacityMask → {id, editing}

[vectorcraft] Enable Opacity Mask
Location: Window › Transparency
Params doc: {id?|ids?}

[vectorcraft] Link Opacity Mask
Location: Window › Transparency
Params doc: {id?|ids?}

[vectorcraft] New Opacity Masks Are Clipping
Location: Window › Transparency
Params doc: {value?} → {value}

[vectorcraft] New Opacity Masks Are Inverted
Location: Window › Transparency
Params doc: {value?} → {value}

[vectorcraft] Page Isolated Blending
Location: Window › Transparency
Params doc: {value?} make the page an isolated group (default: toggle): blend modes of top-level objects don't blend with what lies under the page; saved with the document and written to PDF → {value}

[vectorcraft] Page Knockout Group
Location: Window › Transparency
Params doc: {value?} make the page a knockout group (default: toggle): its layers (the contents of neutral layers) hide what they cover instead of showing it through their transparency; saved with the document and written to PDF → {value}

[vectorcraft] New Sublayer…
Location: Window › Layers
Params doc: {parent?: layer id (default: the highlighted row's layer, else the current layer), name?, options as layer.new} a sublayer on top of the parent's contents → {id}

[vectorcraft] Delete Selection
Location: Window › Layers
Params doc: {ids?|id?} delete rows: layers, sublayers, groups or objects with what they hold (default: the highlighted rows, else the current layer). The last layer stays → {deleted}

[vectorcraft] Duplicate Selection
Location: Window › Layers
Params doc: {ids?|id?} copy rows (default: the highlighted rows, else the current layer), each just above its original; a layer's copy is named `<name> copy`. The copies are highlighted → {ids}

[vectorcraft] Collect in New Layer
Location: Window › Layers
Params doc: {ids?} move rows (default: the highlighted rows, else the selected objects) into a new layer where the topmost of them was (a sublayer when they are in a layer), deselecting every selected object left hidden or locked (the key object too) → {id}

[vectorcraft] Artboard Options…
Location: Window › Artboards
Params doc: {index, name?, x?, y?, width?, height?, moveArt?: bool (default false; a position-only change moves the contained art with its artboard), scaleArt?: bool (Scale Artwork with Artboard: resized, the artboard takes the art fully inside it (locked and hidden art only with lockedAndHidden?: bool, default prefs moveLockedWithArtboard) and its guides from its old rectangle onto the new one, each side by its own ratio; strokes/corners/patterns as object.scale)} → null, or with scaleArt {scaled: the art scaled}

[vectorcraft] Make/Release Clipping Mask
Location: Window › Layers
Params doc: {id?: layer or group (default: the one highlighted layer or group row, else the one selected group, else the current layer)} make: its top object (a path, compound path or text, which loses its paint) clips the rest and moves to the bottom (new art added on top is clipped); release: it stops clipping, the clipping path stays unpainted → {clip}

[vectorcraft] Paste Remembers Layers
Location: Window › Layers
Params doc: {on?} (default: toggle) the document option: on, the Paste commands put objects back into the layers they were copied from (by name; a missing one is made on top), off into the current layer; one undo step when it changes (document.inspect → pasteRemembersLayers) → {on}

[vectorcraft] Merge Selected
Location: Window › Layers
Params doc: {ids?} (default: the highlighted rows) merge two or more rows into the layer listed (highlighted) last: the other layers' contents and the other rows move into it, keeping their stacking order, and the emptied layers go. Every selected object left hidden or locked, such as one merged into a hidden or locked layer, is deselected (the key object too). One undo step → {id}

[vectorcraft] Flatten Artwork
Location: Window › Layers
Params doc: {id?} (default: the highlighted row's top-level layer, else the current one's) move the art of every other visible top-level layer into this one, keeping the stacking order; hidden layers and their art are deleted, template layers stay. Every selected object left hidden or locked, such as one flattened into a locked layer, is deselected (the key object too). One undo step → {id, discarded}

[vectorcraft] Release to Layers (Sequence)
Location: Window › Layers
Params doc: {id?: layer or group (default: the highlighted row, else the current layer), build?: bool} each object in it goes into a new sublayer of its own, in stacking order (a group's objects go into sublayers of its layer, where the group was). `build`: Release to Layers (Build), each new sublayer holds copies of the objects up to its own, so the layers add up. One undo step → {ids}

[vectorcraft] Release to Layers (Build)
Location: Window › Layers
Params doc: {id?} layer.releaseToLayers with build: true → {ids}

[vectorcraft] Template
Location: Window › Layers
Params doc: {ids?, on?: bool (default: toggle the first)} make layers templates (locked, dimmed, left out of print and export) or ordinary layers again (layer.setProps template) → {on}

[vectorcraft] Hide Others
Location: Window › Layers
Params doc: {ids?} hide every top-level layer but those holding the highlighted rows (else the current layer), which show. One undo step → {count}

[vectorcraft] Show All Layers
Location: Window › Layers
Params doc: {} show every layer and sublayer → {count}

[vectorcraft] Outline Others
Location: Window › Layers
Params doc: {ids?} turn Preview off (outline view) for every top-level layer but those holding the highlighted rows (else the current layer), which preview → {count}

[vectorcraft] Preview All Layers
Location: Window › Layers
Params doc: {} turn Preview on for every layer and sublayer → {count}

[vectorcraft] Lock Others
Location: Window › Layers
Params doc: {ids?} lock every top-level layer but those holding the highlighted rows (else the current layer), which unlock → {count}

[vectorcraft] Unlock All Layers
Location: Window › Layers
Params doc: {} unlock every layer and sublayer → {count}

[vectorcraft] Locate Object
Location: Window › Layers
Params doc: {id?} (default: the last selected object) highlight the object's row; the Layers panel opens the layers around it and scrolls to it → {id, ancestry: [layer…, id]}

[vectorcraft] Remove Anchor Points
Location: Object › Path
Params doc: {} remove the direct-selected anchors without opening their paths, refitting the curve round each → {removedObjects}

[vectorcraft] Expand Appearance
Location: Object
Params doc: {ids?: [..], target?} turn each object's appearance into objects: every fill and stroke becomes an object of its own (strokes outlined, brushed strokes their brush art) grouped in paint order under the object's id and transparency, geometry effects are baked, raster effects become an embedded image (shadows and outer glows below the art; blur, feather and inner glow replace it), type with effects or fills of its own is outlined; Crop Marks become a group of the object and its marks; a group's or layer's own fills and strokes become objects among its members, which are expanded too. Hidden fills, strokes and effects are dropped. Enabled when a selected or targeted object's appearance isn't basic (`ids` then pick which objects) → {ids}

[vectorcraft] Crop
Location: Window › Pathfinder
Params doc: {} operate on the selected objects (back → front) → {ids}

[vectorcraft] Clean Up…
Location: Object › Path
Params doc: {strayPoints?: true, unpaintedObjects?: true, emptyTextPaths?: true} → {removed}

[vectorcraft] Create Trim Marks
Location: Object
Params doc: {style?: "roman"|"japanese" (default: the japaneseCropMarks preference; japanese: double lines at the trim and bleed edges plus centre marks), allArtboards?: bool (default: true when nothing is selected), offset?: pt (9, roman), length?: pt (18), bleed?: pt (8.5, japanese), weight?: pt (0.3)} trim marks stroked in [Registration] (printing on every plate) around the selection, or around every artboard, one group each, as one undo step → {id: the first group, ids}

[vectorcraft] Rearrange All Artboards…
Location: Object › Artboards
Params doc: {layout?: gridByRow|gridByColumn|row|column (gridByRow; byColumn?: true is gridByColumn), order?: leftToRight|rightToLeft (leftToRight: right-to-left mirrors the order along the rows), columns?: n (2; the rows for gridByColumn; row and column ignore it), spacing?: pt (20), moveArtwork?: true (locked and hidden art only with prefs moveLockedWithArtboard), patterns?: bool (Transform Patterns: pattern fills and strokes transform with the art; default: prefs transformPatternTiles)} lay the artboards out in their order, the grid's top-left at the first artboard's → {artboards, rows, columns}

[vectorcraft] Blend Options…
Location: Object › Blend
Params doc: {spacing?: smooth|steps|distance, value?: n, steps?: n, distance?: pt, orientation?: page|path} set the options of the selected blends; with no blend selected, the options new blends start with (a tool setting, not an undo step) → {defaults?: true}

[vectorcraft] Assign Profile…
Location: Edit
Params doc: {rgb?: profile|null, cmyk?: profile|null} tag the document with profiles (colour numbers are kept) → {rgb, cmyk}

[vectorcraft] Overprint Black…
Location: Edit › Edit Colors
Params doc: {remove?: false, percentage?: 100, fill?: true, stroke?: true, includeCmyBlacks?: false, includeSpotBlacks?: false, ids?} make the black fills and/or strokes of the selection (or ids; groups: their contents; type: its characters) overprint, or stop (remove). Black: K ≥ percentage with no C, M or Y (any with includeCmyBlacks), not linked to a spot swatch (unless includeSpotBlacks); a gradient is black when every stop is → {changed: objects}

[vectorcraft] Smart Punctuation…
Location: Type
Params doc: {quotes?: true (straight quotes become the Document Setup quotes), dashes?: true (-- → en dash, --- → em dash), ellipsis?: true (... → …), scope?: "selection"|"document"} → {changed}

[vectorcraft] Find Next
Location: Edit
Params doc: {find, matchCase?, wholeWord?} select the next text object (after the selected one, wrapping) containing `find` → {id|null}

[vectorcraft] Insert Inline Symbol
Location: Type
Params doc: {id?: text id (default: the text the Type tool edits), at?: byte offset (default: the Type tool's selection, which it replaces; clamped to the text), symbol?: symbol name (default: the Symbols panel's current symbol), scale?: art height ÷ font size = 1 (0 < scale ≤ 100), shift?: pt raise = 0} place a document symbol inline in the text as one character (U+FFFC) that flows like a glyph: its art is scaled to `scale` × the font size tall, its vertical centre on the middle of the cap height raised by `shift`. Typing, Backspace and Delete over it remove it whole → {id, caret}

[vectorcraft] New Character Style
Location: Window › Type › Character Styles
Params doc: {name?, attrs?: {…}} (default attrs: the selected text's) → {name}

[vectorcraft] Duplicate Character Style
Location: Window › Type › Character Styles
Params doc: {name} → {name}

[vectorcraft] New Paragraph Style
Location: Window › Type › Paragraph Styles
Params doc: {name?, attrs?: {…}} (default attrs: the selected text's) → {name}

[vectorcraft] Duplicate Paragraph Style
Location: Window › Type › Paragraph Styles
Params doc: {name} → {name}

[vectorcraft] ArtCraft Website
Location: Help
Params doc: {} → {url}

[vectorcraft] Create
Location: Type › Threaded Text
Params doc: {} thread the selected area type (and closed paths, which become frames) in stacking order → {ids}

[vectorcraft] Design…
Location: Object › Graph
Params doc: {new?: name|true (New Design: the selected art becomes a graph design, named "New Design" when true; put a rectangle at the back to set the size it draws at), rename?: name, to?: new name (the graphs drawing it follow), paste?: name (Paste Design: a copy of the design's art into the document, selected, to edit and save again), delete?: name|[names] (graphs drawing them go back to their default marks)}; no params or selectUnused → {designs: [names], unused: [the names no graph draws with]}

[vectorcraft] New View…
Location: View
Params doc: {name?, center: [x, y], zoom: (1 = 100%), rotation?: deg} save a view (the app fills in the current one) → {name, index}

[vectorcraft] Edit Views…
Location: View
Params doc: {name, newName?, delete?: bool} rename or delete a saved view; no params → {views}

[vectorcraft] Edit Opacity Mask
Location: Window › Transparency
Params doc: {id?} edit the mask art of `id` (default: the first selected object with a mask) in place, as clicking the mask thumbnail in the Transparency panel does → {layer}

[vectorcraft] Stop Editing Opacity Mask
Location: Window › Transparency
Params doc: {} leave mask editing (the object thumbnail) → {id}

[vectorcraft] View Opacity Mask
Location: Window › Transparency
Params doc: {on?: bool (default: toggle), id?} show only the opacity mask of `id` (default: the object whose mask is edited, else the first selected object with a mask) on the canvas, as greyscale coverage, and edit it, as Alt-clicking the mask thumbnail does; off shows the artwork again (still editing) → {on, id}

[vectorcraft] Point Text Objects
Location: Select › Object
Params doc: {} → {count}

[vectorcraft] Area Text Objects
Location: Select › Object
Params doc: {} → {count}

[vectorcraft] Brush Strokes
Location: Select › Object
Params doc: {} → {count}

[vectorcraft] Bristle Brush Strokes
Location: Select › Object
Params doc: {} objects whose brush name contains "bristle" → {count}

[vectorcraft] Recall Selection
Location: Select
Params doc: {name} select the objects of a saved selection, leaving out those deleted since and those that are hidden or locked, inside a hidden or locked object or layer, on a template layer, or outside the isolated group or layer → {count}

[vectorcraft] Lock Guides
Location: View › Guides
Shortcut: Cmd+Alt+;
Params doc: {locked?: bool} toggle (or set) the session's guide lock → {locked}

[vectorcraft] Clear Guides
Location: View › Guides
Params doc: {} delete all ruler guides and guide paths → {count}

[vectorcraft] Document Color Mode
Location: File › Document Color Mode
Params doc: {mode: "cmyk"|"rgb", convert?: true (convert every colour of the art, symbols, pattern tiles and swatches through the colour settings; swatch links kept; Gray colours stay Gray, on the black plate), intent?, grays?: "profile" (default: RGB greys separate through the CMYK profile like any colour, into four-colour greys and a rich black) | "black" (to CMYK, RGB greys with R = G = B go on the black plate only, K = their grey value)} → {changed}

[vectorcraft] Bind Variable
Location: Window › Variables
Params doc: {variable, ids?} bind objects (default: the selection) to a variable; text needs type, locked art is refused. An object may hold several variables, and binding it to one it already has changes nothing → {bound, already}

[vectorcraft] Edit Data Set…
Location: Window › Variables
Params doc: {name, values?: {variable: value}} replace a dataset's values; a variable left out loses its value in this row → {values, removed}

[vectorcraft] Select Data Set
Location: Window › Variables
Params doc: {name} apply a dataset in one undo step, deselecting every selected object left hidden or locked (the key object too) → {applied, skipped}

[vectorcraft] Document Info
Location: Window › Document Info
Params doc: {selectionOnly?, category?: document|objects|graphicStyles|spotColors|patterns|gradients|symbols|fonts|fontDetails|linkedImages|embeddedImages (only that one in sections and the text), format?: "text" (→ {text}: the report Document Info › Save… and Package write)} → {document, objects: {paths, compoundPaths, groups, …}, fonts, images, swatches, graphicStyleNames (with selectionOnly: the styles the selected objects are linked to), …, sections: [{id, title, rows: [[label, value]]}] (the panel's categories; fontDetails: each font's file and whether its licence lets it be embedded)}

[vectorcraft] Duplicate Artboard
Location: Window › Artboards
Params doc: {index?: n (default: the Artboard tool's artboard), art?: bool (default: the Artboard tool's moveArt option), patterns?: bool (Transform Patterns: pattern fills and strokes transform with the art; default: prefs transformPatternTiles)} copy placed right of the last artboard, with copies of the art fully inside it when `art` (locked and hidden art only with prefs moveLockedWithArtboard) → {index, ids: the art's copies}

[vectorcraft] Merge
Location: Object › Live Paint
Params doc: {ids?} add the other selected paths (and Live Paint groups) to the first Live Paint group, keeping its paint → {id, faces, edges}

[vectorcraft] Release
Location: Object › Live Paint
Params doc: {id?} replace Live Paint groups with their original paths → {ids}

[vectorcraft] Expand
Location: Object › Live Paint
Params doc: {id?} turn Live Paint groups into plain groups of their painted faces and edges → {ids}

[vectorcraft] Make
Location: Object › Image Trace
Params doc: {id?: image or Image Trace group (default: selection), preset?: name (imageTrace.presets), params?: {mode: "blackAndWhite"|"grayscale"|"color"|"logo", threshold: 0-255, palette: "limited"|"fullTone"|"automatic"|"documentLibrary" (color mode; limited: the `colors` best colours, fullTone: as many as the tones need, more with colorDetail, automatic: flat art with its own colours, else fullTone, documentLibrary: at most `colors` of the library's colours, as they are), colors: 2-256, colorDetail: 0-100 (fullTone, automatic), library: "document" (the document's swatches) or a swatch library id or name (swatch.library.list; documentLibrary), paths: 0-100, corners: 0-100, noise: px, method: "abutting"|"overlapping", ignoreWhite, snapCurvesToLines, fills: true, strokes: false (Create: lines up to strokeWidth wide become stroked centre lines; without fills, wider areas become stroked outlines), strokeWidth: px (10), logoColors?: ["#rrggbb"…] (mode logo: flat-colour logos only; colours found automatically or named here, white is always its own colour, at most ten; noise = areas under noise/10 px ignored; edges to a fraction of a pixel, sharp corners restored, lines and circles snapped; enclosed transparent areas are painted white unless ignoreWhite makes them holes; fills/strokes are ignored; gradients and photos are refused)}, view?: as imageTrace.setView (default: the traced object's own, else tracingResult)} → {id, paths, anchors, colors}

